=== SIGNATURE ===
first_time(arr)

=== COMMENT ===
For each cell, 1 if that value appears for the first time when arr is read in row-major order, 0 if it repeats an earlier value. Output is the same size and shape as arr.

=== CODE ===
=LAMBDA(arr,
  LET(
    cols, COLUMNS(arr),
    flat, TOCOL(arr),
    n_items, ROWS(flat),
    first_seen, --(XMATCH(flat, flat) = SEQUENCE(n_items)),
    WRAPROWS(first_seen, cols)
  )
)

=== DESCRIPTION ===
Flags the first appearance of each distinct value. Reading arr in row-major order (left to right, top to bottom), a cell is 1 the first time its value is seen and 0 for every later repeat. The returned array has the same size and shape as arr.

Arguments:
  arr - a single value or a 1D/2D array.

Returns:
  An array the same size and shape as arr, of 1s (first occurrence) and 0s (repeat).

How it works: the input is flattened row-major, XMATCH finds the first position of each value, and a cell is 1 exactly where that first position equals the cell's own position. The flags are wrapped back into arr's shape with WRAPROWS.

Numbers and text are compared exactly (5 and "5" are different). Blank cells read as 0.

Examples:
  first_time({"A";"B";"A";"C";"B"})   ->  {1;1;0;1;0}
  first_time({"A","B","A";"C","A","B"}) ->  {1,1,0;1,0,0}
